# What must NOT reach the build context.
#
# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything here is sent to the daemon and
# lands in an intermediate layer. The final stage is scratch and copies only the
# two binaries out, so none of it ships -- but an intermediate layer is still a
# readable copy of whatever went in, cached on the build host.
#
# dev_config is the sharp one: it holds a live Anthropic API key, the session
# and secret keys, and a database of encrypted mail passwords. None of it is
# needed to compile anything.
dev_config/
pepper.txt
.env

# The pepper arrives as --build-arg PEPPER, never as a file, and a pepper.txt
# in the context would be the wrong one anyway.

# 101MB of PHP that nothing in the build reads. It is a reference checkout kept
# beside the source, and sending it makes every build slower for no reason.
snappymail/

# Not read by the build, and .git is the largest of them.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.claude/

# The host's own build output. Rebuilt inside the image from source, so a copy
# from the host is at best wasted bytes and at worst a stale binary somebody
# later mistakes for the built one.
/starry_go_mail
/mailctl
/funcsdoc
web_proto_worker
st_claude

# Documentation and scratch.
*.md
things_to_do_1.txt
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# NOT ignored, and must not be: src/mail_client.json.example and src/schema.sql
# are //go:embed-ed (see src/seed.go and src/db.go), so a build without them does
# not compile. An embed path cannot contain "..", which is why those two data
# files live under src/ with the code rather than at the root with the docs.
